# Cell from playpick: mode=raid, boss=gorged (The Bloodgorged), spec=paladin:holy,
# style=wander, size=25, difficulty=heroic, view=844x390,touch, save=fresh.
#
# gorged is the fourth boss (encounterIndex 3, src/sim/encounters.ts) and a
# fresh save starts at unlocked=0 -- only Bonegrinder 10N is open on the raid
# setup screen (confirmed this session: `targets` on setup showed only
# size/difficulty pickers, no boss row at all, matching src/progress.ts's
# comment that the setup screen no longer names a boss). The invite hash is
# the documented way in regardless (docs/playtest.md's own #b=marrow&s=10&h=1
# example): src/main.ts's invite handler unlocks the tier a link names on
# purpose ("the chain is there so a new player meets the game in order, not
# to stop somebody being invited past it"), so #b=gorged&s=25&h=1 opens
# straight onto the roster with that fight chosen. That hash also lands
# directly on `roster`, not `raid` setup, so there is no `next` button there
# -- a harmless no-such-control the first run of this script hit.
#
# First holy paladin this job has played, first `play wander` inside an
# actual boss pull rather than steering an `evening` between rooms (wander
# has only appeared twice before, both mode=clear), and the hardest cell
# playpick has handed a healer spec into yet at 25-heroic. Extended past the
# first run's 150s (which left the boss at 9%, ongoing) to see an outcome.
open #b=gorged&s=25&h=1
tap class:paladin:holy
tap pull
waitscreen fight 20
state
play wander 220
state
bill
shot end
